WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:08.360
A group policy may begin at headquarters, but it has to remain defensible
across jurisdictions, legal entities and lines of business.

00:08.360 --> 00:17.515
Before a policy is approved, a control is attested or an assurance opinion is
formed, reviewers need the governing source, the applicable wording and

00:17.515 --> 00:20.185
a clear record of what was checked.

00:20.185 --> 00:26.670
When that evidence is fragmented across a multinational document estate,
documentary uncertainty becomes operational and regulatory risk.

00:27.670 --> 00:31.060
A large bank does not work from one document.

00:31.060 --> 00:37.086
Group policy connects to local addenda, procedures, control descriptions,
approved exceptions, change records and external requirements.

00:37.086 --> 00:43.112
The same policy family may apply differently by country, regulator, legal
entity, product or effective date.

00:43.112 --> 00:46.501
A local requirement can add to the group minimum.

00:46.501 --> 00:49.514
An exception can change the route to approval.

00:49.514 --> 00:55.541
A cited source can be replaced while the policy that depends on it remains in
circulation.

00:55.541 --> 00:58.554
The review problem is not simply finding words.

00:58.554 --> 01:01.190
It is establishing the relationships between them.

01:02.190 --> 01:04.768
The credible starting point is bounded.

01:04.768 --> 01:10.353
Select one policy family, a small number of jurisdictions and representative
legal entities.

01:10.353 --> 01:18.516
Agree the authoritative corpus: the current group policy and revision history,
local addenda, public regulator material, cleared procedures and

01:18.516 --> 01:22.812
control descriptions, and the approved record of exceptions and
interpretations.

01:22.812 --> 01:30.975
Define which questions the evaluation will test, who can see the material, and
who is authorised to decide applicability.

01:30.975 --> 01:36.990
Cortessa is evaluated inside that agreed scope; it does not claim universal
regulatory coverage.

01:37.990 --> 01:44.168
Cortessa is intended to run on a dedicated sovereign workstation inside an
agreed boundary.

01:44.168 --> 01:50.346
The approved corpus, local index, on-device model and source viewer remain
within that environment.

01:50.346 --> 01:54.759
Runtime operation does not depend on a public cloud service.

01:54.759 --> 02:00.055
The bank defines the permitted documents, users, identity controls and
security posture.

02:00.055 --> 02:05.350
Cortessa supports evidence review without widening access or becoming the
policy owner.

02:06.350 --> 02:10.915
Ask lets a reviewer question the approved document set in natural language.

02:10.915 --> 02:14.719
The useful result is not fluent prose on its own.

02:14.719 --> 02:23.850
It is an answer tied to inspectable source passages, so the reviewer can open
the document, read the surrounding wording and check the effective

02:23.850 --> 02:24.230
context.

02:24.230 --> 02:29.176
Where the cited evidence supports the wording, the route to source is visible.

02:29.176 --> 02:36.784
Where it does not, policy can keep the response in Draft or withhold it rather
than present it as verified.

02:36.784 --> 02:37.925
Verified establishes provenance.

02:37.925 --> 02:42.110
It does not establish legal interpretation, policy correctness or
jurisdictional applicability.

02:43.110 --> 02:48.395
Audit works across the selected corpus rather than waiting for one question at
a time.

02:48.395 --> 02:56.851
It can surface an addendum that cites a source the corpus does not hold, a
group clause without an inspectable route to authority, inconsistent

02:56.851 --> 03:01.783
terminology or dates, revision uncertainty, or an unexplained divergence
between group and local wording.

03:01.783 --> 03:05.659
Each result must lead back to the passage that created it.

03:05.659 --> 03:13.057
The reviewer can inspect the source, determine whether the discrepancy is real
and record the outcome through the bank's existing process.

03:13.057 --> 03:15.524
A surfaced discrepancy is a review question.

03:15.524 --> 03:17.990
It is not a finding of non-compliance.

03:18.990 --> 03:23.763
A multinational bank cannot outsource local interpretation to a language
model.

03:23.763 --> 03:29.404
The relevant legal entity, jurisdiction, regulator, policy state and effective
date all matter.

03:29.404 --> 03:38.515
Local compliance and legal specialists determine what applies, how an apparent
conflict should be resolved, and whether an exception is valid.

03:38.515 --> 03:41.987
Cortessa makes the evidence route and uncertainty visible.

03:41.987 --> 03:44.590
The authorised specialist makes the judgement.

03:45.590 --> 03:50.870
The first line owns the business activity, its controls and its operational
evidence.

03:50.870 --> 03:56.150
The second line sets the framework, oversees risk and challenges
interpretation or implementation.

03:56.150 --> 04:00.212
The third line independently assesses the framework and the evidence.

04:00.212 --> 04:06.304
Cortessa can support source investigation and traceability for each line,
while preserving their separate responsibilities.

04:06.304 --> 04:11.990
It does not become the control owner, the compliance authority or the internal
auditor.

04:12.990 --> 04:16.050
The operating picture should show more than an answer.

04:16.050 --> 04:22.510
Reviewers need the source route, the document state and the policy governing
what the system is allowed to present.

04:22.510 --> 04:26.590
Identity, document currency, assertion policy and egress posture are visible
governance concerns.

04:26.590 --> 04:33.390
Audit activity can be recorded in a local ledger so the organisation can
inspect what the system did and when.

04:33.390 --> 04:36.110
That record can support an assurance evidence package.

04:36.110 --> 04:41.550
It does not make every conclusion correct, and it does not replace the bank's
approval record.

04:42.550 --> 04:47.750
The right first engagement is a bounded paid evaluation, not a theatre
demonstration.

04:47.750 --> 04:50.950
Compare matched tasks against the bank's current workflow.

04:50.950 --> 04:58.550
Measure the time to locate and inspect the governing source, reviewer effort,
accepted and rejected findings, false-finding burden, unanswered

04:58.550 --> 05:00.550
questions, traceability and evidence-package completeness.

05:00.550 --> 05:03.750
Include difficult documents, conflicting wording and absent sources.

05:03.750 --> 05:08.150
Record corpus preparation and setup effort as part of the result.

05:08.150 --> 05:14.950
The evaluation should show where Cortessa helps, where it fails and what must
change before any expansion.

05:15.950 --> 05:18.454
Observed failures become bounded development work.

05:18.454 --> 05:25.967
Retrieval gaps, document handling, access requirements and workflow friction
are remediated and retested against the agreed task set.

05:25.967 --> 05:35.150
The outcome is an evidence package for the next decision: whether the workflow
merits further hardening, a wider corpus or another jurisdiction.

05:35.150 --> 05:40.576
Cortessa claims no bank deployment, regulator approval, complete obligation
mapping or guaranteed saving.

05:40.576 --> 05:44.750
The value has to be demonstrated in the customer's environment.

05:45.750 --> 05:47.548
Bring one policy family.

05:47.548 --> 05:48.897
Select the jurisdictions.

05:48.897 --> 05:50.695
Agree the evidence standard.

05:50.695 --> 05:55.190
Start a conversation about a scoped global-banking evaluation with Cortessa.
